*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env

# Session artefacts, not project files. HANDOFF.md IS tracked on purpose:
# it records verified state and open items for the next session.
HANDOFF.local.md
*.log

# The torch service's virtualenv. 899 MB of wheels, and the whole point of
# the split is that the app does not depend on it -- committing it would make
# the repository carry a dependency it claims not to have, and would bloat
# every clone by a gigabyte. Recreate with:
#   python3 -m venv .venv-torch
#   .venv-torch/bin/pip install torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
.venv-torch/
.venv*/
venv/
env/

# MQL5 compiled output. A .ex5 is tied to the MetaEditor build that produced
# it -- rebuild with scripts/build_mt5_ea.py after a terminal update. Only
# the .mq5 source is tracked.
*.ex5
*.ex4

# Build artifacts that escaped into the repo root as literal-backslash
# filenames, e.g. "\tmp\mt5build-1_5b8aw2\build.log". On Linux that is one
# file whose name contains backslashes, not a path -- the Windows fallback in
# scripts/build_mt5_ea.py that produced them has since been removed, but
# *.log and *.ex5 below would hide them from `git status` again if one ever
# reappears. Listed explicitly so a stray artifact can never present as a
# clean tree.
*\tmp\mt5build-*
*mt5build-*
data/wallets/*.json
data/wallets/*seed*.json
